1.4 
Document Structure 

The ANS SMS Manual consist of 2 documents:  
 ANSM 4 - SMM contains standard safety procedures applicable to all ATS 
units; and  
 ATS SMM contains detailed procedures to be employed by each ATS unit 
with any applicable limitations. 
Note1. - The provisions and procedures required to be included in ATS SMM are 
contained in the CAD 19 - Safety Management. 
Note2. - ATS SMM shall be submitted to the Director of BNA as part of the SMS 
acceptance processes under the provisions of Regulations 167 of the CAR 2016.  
Note3. - Guidance on implementation of an SMS is contained in the CAGM 1902. 
Note4. - ATS SMM shall be reviewed by ATS Deputy Director/Manager, verified 
by Safety Manager and endorsed by the DCEO(ANS).

