Head of SMS Unit, ASQ 

The Head of SMS Unit is responsible to the Director/Deputy Director of ASQ 
for the performance of the SMS and for the delivery of safety services to other 
units within CAAM. 

The Head of SMS Unit advises the Director/Deputy Director of ASQ on safety 
management matters, and is responsible for coordinating and communicating 
safety issues within CAAM as well as with external stakeholders of the aviation 
community. 

The Head of SMS Unit ensures prompt collection and analysis of safety data 
and appropriate distribution within the ATSP related to safety information, as 
necessary. 

The Head of SMS Unit is responsible for: 
 Managing the SMS implementation plan; 
 Managing the operation of the SMS; 

Collecting and analysing safety information in a timely manner; 
 Administering any safety-related surveys; 
 Monitoring and evaluating the results of corrective actions; 

Providing periodic reports on ATSP’s safety performance; 
 Performing/facilitating hazard identification and safety risk analysis; 
 Ensuring that SRA are conducted, if applicable; 

Maintaining SMS documentation and records; 

Planning and facilitating staff safety training;

