The ATSP Safety Officer advises the Responsible Officer or his representative 
on safety matters, and is responsible for coordinating and communicating 
safety issues within his respective unit as well as with external stakeholders 
applicable to the operational functions of the unit. 

The ATSP Safety Officer is authorised under the direction of the Responsible 
Officer to conduct investigations of safety events in accordance with the 
procedures specified in the SMS documentation. 

The ATSP Safety Officer shall act as a proactive focal point for safety issues 
and act as a safety coordinator, if applicable when there is no safety coordinator 
has been appointed. 

The ATSP Safety Officer is responsible for: 
 Managing the SMS implementation plan; 
 Managing the operation of the SMS; 

Collecting and analysing safety information in a timely manner; 
 Monitoring his unit’s operational safety performance; 
 Facilitating ANS quality audit conduct by the ASQ; 

Reviewing internal quality audit report and take necessary corrective 
actions as required; 
 Conducting appropriate SRA, if applicable; 
 Identifying the implementation of appropriate safety risk control strategies; 

Assessing the safety impact related to the introduction of operational 
changes or new technologies; 

Maintaining SMS documentation and records;

