Broadcasts shall be brief and concise and if practicable, of a duration of not more 
than 30 seconds. Messages shall be composed so that pilots can readily 
understand them. 

Each message broadcast shall be consecutively coded starting each day with the 
phonetic alphabet “ALPHA” and continuing until all phonetics are used up. 
